{"author": "ValWood", "body": "* **ARBA rule (ID and label):**\n\n\nGO:0000028 | ribosomal small subunit assembly | IEA with ARBA00088828\n\n\n* **Sequences with problematic annotation (ID + gene/protein name):**\n\nhttps://www.pombase.org/gene/SPBC839.05c rps1701\nhttps://www.pombase.org/gene/SPCC24B10.09 rps1702\n\n* **Description of issue**\n\nThis annotation is from, \nhttps://www.yeastgenome.org/reference/S000051019\n\nbut RPS17A/B do not appear to have a role in \"[ribosomal small subunit assembly](https://www.yeastgenome.org/go/GO:0000028)\" since they are themselves part of the SSU?\n\nAddition of extra copies of rp51 genes led to extra rp51 protein synthesis. The additional rp51 protein was rapidly degraded\n\nCC @edwong57 ", "created_at": "2025-06-12T18:15:33Z", "key": "issue", "labels": ["ARBA", "ARBA - checked"], "state": "closed", "state_reason": "completed", "title": "GO:0000028\t ribosomal small subunit assembly IEA with ARBA00088828", "type": "issue", "updated_at": "2026-08-07T11:45:58Z"}
